  "stories": [
    {
      "id": "story-1",
      "title": "Chasing the Blue Hour in Old Quarters",
      "slug": "chasing-blue-hour",
      "excerpt": "How waking up before sunrise taught me to look for light where everyone else sees empty streets.",
      "content": "Photography is less about the camera you hold and more about how patient you are with the light. \n\nDuring my winter trip through the older lanes of the city, I gave myself a single rule: don't take the camera out until the city is half-awake and the street lamps begin fighting the morning dawn.\n\nThe result was a collection of quiet frames that felt intimate and suspended in time. The smell of fresh filter coffee, the faint hum of temple bells in the distance, and the soft blue mist creeping between heritage buildings. Every frame from that morning carries a memory I can still vividly recall.",
      "coverImage": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509198397868-475647b2a1e5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=80",
      "date": "February 2026",
      "readTime": "3 min read",
      "location": "Old Quarters",
      "likes": 86
    },
    {
      "id": "story-2",
      "title": "The Art of the 35mm Focal Length",
      "slug": "art-of-35mm",
      "excerpt": "Why one single lens has remained glued to my camera body for over three years.",
      "content": "If I had to document the rest of my life with just one lens, it would unquestionably be a fast 35mm.\n\nA 50mm feels like a thoughtful conversation. An 85mm feels like admiring someone from across the room. But a 35mm? A 35mm puts you right in the center of the scene. It forces you to take two steps forward, to engage with your subject, and to include the environment that gives context to the moment.\n\nIt is wide enough to capture architecture and landscape, yet fast and close enough to shoot intimate environmental portraits with beautiful separation. Here are some of my favorite frames shot entirely on this focal length.",
      "coverImage": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1514565131-fce0801e5785?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=80",
      "date": "January 2026",
      "readTime": "4 min read",
      "location": "Everywhere",
      "likes": 112
    }
  ],
